  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Phobia feels like a natural next choice because I want heavy riffs with strong melodic hooks, which connects with my interest in Ten Thousand Fists and One Day Remains.",
    "Mezmerize and Hypnotize offer aggression, melody, and rhythmic changes that appeal to me, while Every Man For Himself gives me a familiar connection to The Reason."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's raw, abrasive sound misses the balance of heaviness and melody I want right now; heavy guitars alone do not make something an immediate choice.",
    "If Only You Were Lonely's emo direction and Hauruck's industrial electronics feel farther from the guitar-led hard rock and metal I am seeking on this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad connection to heavy or alternative music as enough, even though the sound and balance of melody matter to my choice.",
    "My interest in aggressive music seems to have been stretched into an interest in abrasive sounds generally, despite my preference right now for memorable hooks alongside the intensity."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists and One Day Remains makes melodic, riff-driven heaviness especially appealing right now.",
    "Something can fit my taste without being what I would choose today: Fallen interests me but feels lighter than I want, while Death Magnetic interests me but comes after the melodic hard-rock choices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music but sometimes overlook the particular balance of riffs, melody, and intensity that drives my choices right now."
